  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN and a (000-indexed) binary string AAA having length N+1N+1N+1.\n\nFind any permutation PPP of 0,1,2,...,N−1{0,1,2,...,N-1}0,1,2,...,N−1 (or determine that it does not exist) that satisfies the following conditions for all iii (0≤i≤N0 \\le i \\le N0≤i≤N):\n\n\nif Ai=0A_i = 0Ai​=0: No contiguous segment of PPP has mex\\texttt{mex}mex equal to iii\nif Ai=1A_i = 1Ai​=1: There exists at least one contiguous segment of PPP that has mex\\texttt{mex}mex equal to iii\nIf multiple permutations exist that satisfy the given conditions, print any.\n\nNote: mex\\texttt{mex}mex of a segment is the smallest non-negative number that does not occur in that segment.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains the number of test cases TTT. Description of the test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains the binary string AAA of length N+1N + 1N+1.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case print :\n\n\n\nYes\\texttt{Yes}Yes if there exists a permutation PPP that satisfies the conditions described in the statement, followed by the permutation PPP in the next line (If multiple permutations exist that satisfy the given conditions, print any).\nNo\\texttt{No}No otherwise.\n\nYou may print each character of Yes\\texttt{Yes}Yes and No\\texttt{No}No in uppercase or lowercase (for example, yes\\texttt{yes}yes, yEs\\texttt{yEs}yEs, YES\\texttt{YES}YES will be considered identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq  10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤3⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤3⋅105",
      "∣A∣=N+1|A| = N + 1∣A∣=N+1",
      "It is guaranteed that the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
