      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n2\n111\n5\n110100\n5\n110101\n7\n11100111",
        "output": "Yes\n0 1\nNo\nYes\n0 2 1 4 3\nYes\n0 1 3 4 2 5 6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case-1: One of the possible permutations satisfying the given conditions is [0,10, 10,1] because:\n\nmex([1])=0\\texttt{mex}([1]) = 0mex([1])=0. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=0i = 0i=0.\nmex([0])=1\\texttt{mex}([0]) = 1mex([0])=1. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=1i = 1i=1.\nmex([0,1])=2\\texttt{mex}([0, 1]) = 2mex([0,1])=2. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=2i = 2i=2.\n\nTest case-2: It can be proven that no permutation exists that satisfies the given conditions.\nTest case-3: One of the possible permutations satisfying the given conditions is [0,2,1,4,30, 2, 1, 4, 30,2,1,4,3] because:\n\nmex([2])=0\\texttt{mex}([2]) = 0mex([2])=0. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=0i = 0i=0.\nmex([0,2])=1\\texttt{mex}([0, 2]) = 1mex([0,2])=1. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=1i = 1i=1.\nThere does not exist any segment with mex=2\\texttt{mex} = 2mex=2. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=2i = 2i=2.\nmex([0,2,1])=3\\texttt{mex}([0, 2, 1]) = 3mex([0,2,1])=3. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=3i = 3i=3.\nThere does not exist any segment with mex=4\\texttt{mex} = 4mex=4. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=4i = 4i=4.\nmex([0,2,1,4,3])=5\\texttt{mex}([0, 2, 1, 4, 3]) = 5mex([0,2,1,4,3])=5. Therefore the condition is satisfied for i=5i = 5i=5."
